  "rulesMuehleGoal": "Take the other player’s pieces until only 2 are left. Or block their pieces so they cannot move any more.",
  "rulesMuehleTurn": "Each player has 9 pieces. Player 1 starts.\nFirst you take turns putting one piece on a free point.\nOnce all pieces are placed, you slide a piece along a line to the free point next to it.\nWith only 3 pieces left, you may jump: to any free point.",
  "rulesMuehleMill": "3 pieces on one line make a mill. Then you take one of the other player’s pieces.",
  "rulesMuehleSpecial": "Pieces in a mill are safe. Only if all the other player’s pieces are in mills may you take one of them.\nIf you open a mill and close it again, it counts again.\n50 moves in a row without taking a piece (both players counted): a draw.",
  "rulesTrumpfGoal": "Win all the cards. Whoever runs out of cards loses.",
  "rulesTrumpfTurn": "Each player gets 16 cards as a face-down pile. You always play the top card.\nThe player whose turn it is picks a property of their card, for example the speed.\nThe better value wins the round. Usually higher is better, for some properties lower. The card says which.\nThe winner of the round puts both cards under their pile and picks next.\nPlayer 1 picks first.",
  "rulesTrumpfSpecial": "Same value: tie-break! Both cards go into the pot, and the same player picks again. Whoever wins the next round also gets the whole pot.\nAfter 200 rounds, whoever has more cards wins. With the same number it is a draw.\nIf both piles are empty, it is a draw too.",
  "rulesTrumpfPickLow": "3 cards or fewer: choose",
  "rulesTrumpfPickLowText": "With only 2 or 3 cards left, you see all of them and choose which one to play. The picker chooses the card first and then the property. The other player chooses their card after hearing the property.",
  "rulesSetsGoal": "Collect quartets: all 4 cards of a set. Whoever has more quartets at the end wins.",
  "rulesSetsTurn": "Each player gets 8 cards. The other 16 lie face down as the pile.\nAsk the other player for a card you are missing. You must already have a card of that set.\nIf they have the card, they give it to you, and you may ask again.\nIf not, it is a miss: you draw a card from the pile, and it is the other player’s turn.\nPlayer 1 asks first.",
  "rulesSetsSpecial": "With all 4 cards of a set, you lay the quartet down at once.\nIf you draw the card you asked for, it is still the other player’s turn.\nIf you have no cards left, you draw one from the pile.\nWhen all 8 quartets are down, the game is over. 4 to 4 is a draw.",
  "rulesSchiffeGoal": "Sink all the other player’s ships before they sink yours.",
  "rulesSchiffeTurn": "First each player secretly places their fleet on their own sea of 10 by 10 squares. Player 1 starts.\nThen you take turns shooting: tap a square in the other player’s sea.\nYou shoot at each square only once.",
  "rulesSchiffeMiss": "Water: a miss. Now it is the other player’s turn.",
  "rulesSchiffeHit": "Hit! You may shoot again.",
  "rulesSchiffeSunk": "Sunk: every square of the ship is hit. You find out which ship it was.",
  "rulesSchiffeFleet": "The fleet",
  "rulesSchiffeShip": "{count} × {ship} ({length} squares)",
  "rulesSchiffeSpecial": "Ships lie straight: across or up and down.\nShips must not touch, not even at a corner.",
  "rulesGoGoal": "Capture the other player’s flag. You also win if the other player cannot move any more.",
  "rulesGoTurn": "First each player secretly sets up their 40 pieces on their 4 rows. Only the owner sees a piece’s rank.\nPlayer 1 sets up first and moves first.\nOn your turn you move one piece 1 square forward, back, left or right. Never diagonally.\nNo piece can go into the two lakes in the middle.",
  "rulesGoFightTitle": "Who beats whom?",
  "rulesGoFight": "If you move onto the other player’s piece, they fight. Afterwards both players see which pieces they were.\nThe higher rank wins. The loser is out.\nSame rank: both are out.",
  "rulesGoPieces": "The pieces",
  "rulesGoRank": "Rank {rank}",
  "rulesGoCount": "{count} ×",
  "rulesGoMarshal": "The strongest piece. Loses only to the spy, when the spy attacks.",
  "rulesGoScout": "Runs straight over any number of free squares and may attack at the end. If it runs more than 1 square, both players see that it is a scout.",
  "rulesGoMiner": "Defuses bombs: if it attacks one, it takes its place.",
  "rulesGoSpy": "The weakest piece. But if the spy attacks the marshal, the spy wins.",
  "rulesGoBomb": "Never moves. Any attacker is out and the bomb stays. Only the miner defuses it.",
  "rulesGoFlag": "Never moves. Whoever attacks it wins the game.",
  "rulesGoSpecial": "A piece may move back and forth between the same two squares at most 3 times in a row.\nOnce a piece has moved, the other player knows: it is not a bomb and not the flag.\n200 moves in a row without a fight: a draw. Also when nobody can move.",
  "rulesGoZoom": "Zoom the board with two fingers and move it around. The magnifier zooms in on your selected piece; tap it again to see the whole board.",
  "rulesChessGoal": "Checkmate the other player’s king: it is attacked and cannot escape.",
  "rulesChessTurn": "White starts, then you take turns.\nTap one of your pieces and then a square. If one of the other player’s pieces stands there, you capture it.\nOnly the knight may jump over other pieces.",
  "rulesChessPieces": "How the pieces move",
  "rulesChessKing": "1 square in any direction.",
  "rulesChessQueen": "Any distance straight or diagonally.",
  "rulesChessRook": "Any distance straight.",
  "rulesChessBishop": "Any distance diagonally.",
  "rulesChessKnight": "Like an L: 2 squares straight, then 1 to the side. It jumps over pieces.",
  "rulesChessPawn": "1 square forward, on its first move also 2. It captures 1 square diagonally forward.",
  "rulesChessSpecial": "Check: your king is attacked. You must save it at once. A move that leaves your king in check is not allowed.\nCheckmate: the king is in check and cannot be saved. Whoever gives checkmate wins.\nCastling: king and rook have not moved yet, and everything between them is free. The king moves 2 squares towards the rook, the rook jumps next to it. Not allowed while the king is in check or if it would cross an attacked square.\nEn passant: if a pawn moves 2 squares and lands next to your pawn, you may capture it diagonally on your very next move, as if it had moved only 1 square.\nPromotion: when a pawn reaches the last row, it becomes a queen, a rook, a bishop or a knight. You choose.",
  "rulesChessDrawTitle": "Draw",
  "rulesChessDraw": "Stalemate: the player whose turn it is cannot move but is not in check.\nThere are too few pieces left to give checkmate.\nThe same position comes up for the 3rd time.\n75 moves by each player without a capture or a pawn move.\nAgreed draw: the player whose turn it is can offer a draw. The other player accepts or declines.",
  "rulesWordtilesWin": "Whoever has the most points at the end wins.",
  "rulesWordtilesTurn": "You have 7 tiles on your rack.\nLay 1 to 7 tiles in one row or column, with no gap.\nYou score all new words, also the words across them.\nThen you draw tiles from the bag until you have 7 again.",
  "rulesWordtilesChallengeAfter": "The player who challenged then takes their turn as usual.",
  "rulesWordtilesScoreless": "If the game ends because nobody scores any more, everyone loses the points of their remaining tiles.",
  "rulesWordtilesNoRestTitle": "No leftover deduction",
  "rulesWordtilesNoRest": "Nothing is deducted or added at the end: only the words laid count.",
  "rulesMaumauGoal": "Be the first to get rid of all your cards.",
  "rulesMaumauTurn": "There are 32 cards. Each player gets 5, one lies face up in the middle. Player 1 starts.\nPut a card of the same suit or the same value on it, for example hearts on hearts or 9 on 9.\nIf no card fits or you do not want to play one, you draw 1 card. If it fits, you may play it or keep it. If not, it is the other player’s turn.\nWhen the pile is empty, the played cards are shuffled into a new pile.",
  "rulesMaumauJack": "Jack: fits on any card except a jack. You wish for a suit. Then that suit must come next, or a jack.",
  "rulesMaumauSpecial": "The first card in the middle does not count as a special card.\n9, 10, queen and king are normal cards.\nWhoever plays their last card wins, also with a special card.",
  "rulesMaexchenGoal": "Do not lose all your lives. Whoever still has lives at the end wins.",
  "rulesMaexchenTurn": "Roll 2 dice under the cup. Only you see them.\nAnnounce a value. It must be higher than the last announcement. You may also bluff!\nThe other player believes you or doubts.\nIf they believe you, they roll themselves and must announce even higher.\nIf they doubt, the cup is lifted. If the roll is lower than announced, the announcer loses a life. Otherwise the doubter loses one.",
  "rulesMaexchenOrderTitle": "Which roll is higher?",
  "rulesMaexchenOrder": "The higher die counts first: 3 and 1 is 31.\nFrom low to high: 31, 32, 41, 42, 43 and so on up to 65.\nHigher are the doubles: 11, 22, 33, 44, 55, 66.\nThe highest is 21: Mia!",
  "rulesMaexchenSpecial": "The first announcement of a round may be any value.\nIf Mia is announced, you cannot believe it. You doubt, or you give up a life without looking.\nWhoever loses a life starts the next round.\nShaking: instead of tapping “Roll”, you can shake the phone like a cup.",
  "rulesMaexchenLives": "Everyone starts with {count} lives.",
  "shakeConsentTitle": "Roll by shaking?",
  "shakeConsentBody": "Your browser will ask in a moment whether Klunki may sense the phone moving. We only use this for rolling the dice, and it stays on the device.",
  "shakeConsentYes": "Yes, allow shaking",
  "shakeConsentNo": "No, just tap",
  "wordtilesHelp": "How to play",
  "wordtilesHelpJoker": "Swap the blank (rule variant): if you hold the letter a blank on the board stands for, drag it onto the blank. The blank joins your tiles, and you still lay tiles in the same turn (the blank may be one of them). Without laying, the swap does not count. The old word and its points stay.",
  "wordtilesHelpJokerOn": "On in this game.",
  "wordtilesHelpJokerOff": "Off in this game. You can turn it on before a game.",
